# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows checks source out with CRLF by default, and the
# UI test suite reads index.html, web.go and README.md as text and matches
# multi-line source against patterns written with "\n". Those matches found
# nothing on windows-latest and the suite reported that the code had moved,
# while every other platform passed - CI failed exactly that way at a6f5778.
# ui.test.mjs now normalises what it reads as well, so the two guards are
# independent: this one keeps the working tree honest, that one keeps the tests
# honest even if someone checks out with different settings.
#
# Safe to apply wholesale here: every tracked text file is already LF in the
# index (git ls-files --eol), and the repo ships no .bat, .cmd or .ps1 that
# would need CRLF to run.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries Git must never touch. text=auto detects most of these on content,
# but naming them keeps a hand-edited attribute from ever reaching them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
